When the result of a PAD tag is false the part after {app:construct 'else'/} is used.

{pad:page 'constructs/else_1'/}

<hr>The {app:construct 'else'/} construct is a general feature of every PAD tag, it applies to all PAD tags.<br><br>

{common:example 'constructs/else_4'/}

<hr>When the result of a PAD tag is an empty array the part after {app:construct 'else'/} is used.

{pad:page 'constructs/else_2'/}

<hr>The {app:construct 'else'/} context can also be given with the 'else' option at the tag itself.

{pad:page 'constructs/else_3'/}
